Fixed multiple issues in test-bugbot.js:

1. Memory Leak: Stored event listener reference and implemented proper cleanup:
```javascript
const clickHandler = function() { console.log('clicked'); };
document.addEventListener('click', clickHandler);
// Cleanup function
function cleanup() {
  document.removeEventListener('click', clickHandler);
}
```

2. Added null/undefined checks in calculateTotal function to prevent null reference errors.

3. Renamed get_user_Data function to getUserData following camelCase convention.

4. Removed unused variable declaration (const unusedVar = "test").

5. Implemented proper promise error handling with .catch() blocks and HTTP status code checks.

6. Enhanced function robustness with input validation and meaningful error messages.

All security and code quality issues have been addressed, making the file production-ready.
